ENG-02  win32u answers that hardware GPU scheduling (HAGS) is on.

dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c (win32u.so), NtGdiDdDDIQueryAdapterInfo. Lullaby, 2026-10-17 (commit 38d009e).
LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine.

Why: NVIDIA Streamline asks KMTQAITYPE_WDDM_2_7_CAPS and offers DLSS Frame Generation only when
HwSchSupported, HwSchEnabled and HwSchEnabledByDefault are set; D3DMetal runs the generation on Metal and
the Mac's GPU schedules its own work, so the answer is "on" (0x7). Plain DLSS does not need it.
Switch: none (the query is answered the same for every program). Requires: nothing.
Other bases: applies unchanged to all eight WineForge releases (patches/engine/rehearse.sh, 2026-10-18).
Test: patches/engine/tests/d3dkmt-hags-caps.c (D3DKMTQueryAdapterInfo, WDDM_2_7_CAPS: expects 0x7); in a game
with Streamline, the Frame Generation option appears.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c b/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
index ae82a769794..ab7dfe556c4 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/d3dkmt.c
@@ -617,6 +617,20 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtGdiDdDDIQueryAdapterInfo( D3DKMT_QUERYADAPTERINFO *desc )
         *value = KMT_DRIVERVERSION_WDDM_3_1;
         return STATUS_SUCCESS;
     }
+    case KMTQAITYPE_WDDM_2_7_CAPS:
+    {
+        /* D3DKMT_WDDM_2_7_CAPS: HwSchSupported, HwSchEnabled, HwSchEnabledByDefault.
+         * Hardware-accelerated GPU scheduling is what NVIDIA Streamline requires
+         * before it offers DLSS Frame Generation, which D3DMetal runs on Metal; the
+         * Mac's GPU schedules its own work, so the answer is "on". */
+        UINT *value = desc->pPrivateDriverData;
+
+        if (desc->PrivateDriverDataSize < sizeof(*value))
+            return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+
+        *value = 0x7;
+        return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+    }
     default:
     {
         FIXME( "type %d not handled.\n", desc->Type );
